  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry conditions and seasonable temperatures through \nearly next week, with frost possible this weekend.\n\nSurface high pressure remains to the north through Saturday with\ndry conditions and seasonal temperatures expected to continue.\nHigh temperatures today will be in the 60s for most with only\nhighest elevations staying in the 50s. Tonight, low temperatures\nwill be in the upper 30s to 40s. For Friday and Saturday,\nsurface high pressure extends southward from Canada with dry\ncold fronts bringing in cooler air. High temperatures stay in\nthe 50s to low 60s while overnight lows plummet into the 30s for\nmost. The exception will be east of the I-95 corridor where low\ntemperatures stay in the low 40s. Frost is possible Friday and\nSaturday night. \n\nHigh pressure will continue to build southward into the region \nSunday through Tuesday. Dry conditions and seasonable \ntemperatures expected each day with light north to east winds. A\nbackdoor cold front could try to push into the region Tuesday \ninto Tuesday night, but will have very little to no moisture \nwith it to produce any precipitation. A surge of cooler \ntemperatures will follow behind the front for the day on \nWednesday.",
